# REGIONAL GAZETTE OF BIMA CITY

NUMBER:  203                                   YEAR  2018                                SERIES:

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF BIMA CITY

# NUMBER  6  YEAR 2018

# CONCERNING

# PROTECTION OF WOMEN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

# BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

# MAYOR OF BIMA,

Considering:  
a.	that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence;  

that all forms of violence against women constitute violations of human rights so that their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life is guaranteed in accordance with their nature and destiny without discrimination;  

that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women Victims of Violence;  

In View of:	1. 	Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;  

Law Number 69 of 1958 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions Within Level I Regions of Bali, West Nusa Tenggara and East Nusa Tenggara (State Gazette of 1958 Number 122, Supplement to State Gazette Number 1655);  

Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);  

Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 3886);  

Law Number 13 of 2002 concerning the Establishment of Bima City in West Nusa Tenggara Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 26, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4188);  

Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 39, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 4279);  

Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 4419);  

Law Number 39 of 2004 concerning the Placement and Protection of Indonesian Migrant Workers Abroad (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 137, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4447);  

Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning the Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4636);  

Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);  

Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 12, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4976);  

Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);  

Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5659);  

Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation of Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia number 64);  

Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning the Implementation of Women's Protection;  

Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 01 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards (SPM) for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2010 Number 56);  

Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;  

Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning the Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence;  

With Mutual Approval

# REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BIMA CITY

# MAYOR OF BIMA

# DECIDES:

To Establish:	REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE PROTECTION OF WOMEN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE.

